# Keeps the build context small and, more importantly, keeps secrets out of it.
#
# The Dockerfile no longer copies `.env`, but a file in the context can still be
# copied by accident — a future `COPY . .` would pick it up. Excluding it here means
# the daemon never receives it at all.

# ── Secrets ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key

# ── Build output and dependencies ────────────────────────────────────────────
# node_modules is installed inside the image from the lockfile; sending the host's
# copy would both bloat the context and risk shipping platform-specific binaries.
node_modules
dist
coverage
*.tsbuildinfo

# ── Tests and tooling ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
test
**/*.spec.ts
jest.config.js
.eslintrc.js
.prettierrc

# ── Version control and editors ──────────────────────────────────────────────
.git
.gitignore
.github
.vscode
.idea

# ── Docs and local artefacts ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
docs
README.md
Dockerfile
.dockerignore
npm-debug.log*
